cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If this was useful in your work, please cite it."
title: "Reading a subsample against a model-card number: two ZDTaichu5.0-9B benchmarks re-measured on one GPU"
abstract: "Two model-card numbers of ZDTaichu5.0-9B re-measured on a single RTX 4090 under the card's own protocol. Thinking mode was affordable on a uniform random subsample only, so four standard estimators of the full-set accuracy are reported rather than one: direct, difference, regression on the thinking-off census as an auxiliary variable, and post-stratified. CV-Bench lands 88.45 to 89.33 percent, above the card's 86.82; MathVista lands 77.20 to 82.00 percent, below the card's 84.50; every interval contains its card number. The subsample the thinking-on arm could afford runs 5.33 points easier than the rest of MathVista, which is why the estimator matters."
type: software
